  <p>Additional CVE patterns in <code>_G.config.vulnerability.cve_patterns</code> (init.lua): CVE-2024-25600 (Bricks Builder RCE), CVE-2024-27956 (WP Automatic SQLi), CVE-2024-1071 (Ultimate Member SQLi), CVE-2022-0739 (BookingPress SQLi), CVE-2024-2879 (LayerSlider SQLi).</p>

  <h2 id="suricata">Suricata Alert-Based Detections</h2>
  <p>The system leverages Suricata alerts to detect potential exploits. When an alert is generated, it is processed via <code>suricata_rules.lua</code> and used to generate a descriptive reason string mapped to an AbuseIPDB category.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Detection Mechanism:</strong> Suricata signature matching on network traffic (eve.json).</li>
    <li><strong>Reputation Scoring:</strong> Severity 1 → +50, Severity 2 → +25, default → +10. Max score capped at 100.</li>
    <li><strong>Why eve.json:</strong> Previous fast.log regex parser had 8 capture groups into 7 variables — Lua silently drops excess, shifting all fields. eve.json uses named fields, eliminating this bug class.</li>
    <li><strong>Private IP filtering:</strong> <code>is_private_ip()</code> filters RFC1918/loopback at ingestion time.</li>
    <li><strong>Decay:</strong> <code>decayed_score()</code> applies exponential decay at READ time based on half-life, offense count, and permaflag thresholds.</li>
  </ul>

